    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a passion for me, even though I pursued a vocational diploma after school. It’s a subject that combines logic and creativity, which I find deeply satisfying. I enjoy solving problems and seeing patterns, especially in physics, where maths becomes tangible. My parents’ academic background pushed me to appreciate its beauty, but my journey has been more about practical application than theoretical depth.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Anxiety is a constant companion for me, especially with complex topics or time pressure. I’m highly neurotic, so even routine maths tasks can feel overwhelming at times. However, I’ve learned to break problems into smaller steps, which helps manage my stress. It’s exhausting but necessary—I push through because I know the reward is worth it.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I haven’t used AI tools for maths yet, but I’m curious about them. My work as a self-employed cyclist and gardener leaves little time for formal learning, so I rely on my own problem-solving. Still, I’d love to explore AI’s potential—it could make complex topics more accessible without the anxiety of traditional methods.",
